1
00:00:09,622 --> 00:00:14,085
KOCHIKAME

2
00:00:14,293 --> 00:00:17,171
Ah, summer's here again

3
00:00:17,380 --> 00:00:20,091
It's come, it's arrived, it's here

4
00:00:20,299 --> 00:00:23,177
Ah, summer's here again

5
00:00:23,386 --> 00:00:25,763
It's come, it's arrived, here it is!

6
00:00:25,972 --> 00:00:28,975
Big waves, small waves, tiny waves and middle-size waves

7
00:00:29,183 --> 00:00:31,644
Here they come on the southern wind

8
00:00:31,853 --> 00:00:34,897
Big boobs, small boobs, tiny boobs and middle-size boobs

9
00:00:35,106 --> 00:00:37,900
At the beach Jiggle, jiggle, jiggle!

10
00:00:38,109 --> 00:00:40,903
Ah, summer's here again

11
00:00:41,112 --> 00:00:43,906
It's come, it's arrived, it's here

12
00:00:44,115 --> 00:00:46,742
Ah, summer's here again

13
00:00:46,951 --> 00:00:49,412
It's come, it's arrived, it's here already!

14
00:00:49,620 --> 00:00:52,665
Big waves, small waves, tiny waves and middle-size waves

15
00:00:52,874 --> 00:00:55,501
Here they come on the southern wind

16
00:00:55,710 --> 00:00:58,463
Big butts, small butts, tiny butts and middle-size butts

17
00:00:58,671 --> 00:01:02,967
At the beach Bounce, bounce, bounce!

18
00:01:06,095 --> 00:01:15,480
Here they come on the southern wind

19
00:01:17,940 --> 00:01:21,986
Bouncing at the beach Jiggling at the beach

20
00:01:23,279 --> 00:01:24,363
Want you!

21
00:01:28,242 --> 00:01:33,998
I SCREAM FOR SHAVED ICE SKIING!

22
00:01:43,132 --> 00:01:44,550
It's so hot.

23
00:01:44,884 --> 00:01:47,470
How can it be this hot so early in the morning?

24
00:01:47,678 --> 00:01:49,347
"ICE"

25
00:01:49,555 --> 00:01:51,641
"KURODA'S SWEETS AND SHAVED ICE"

26
00:01:51,849 --> 00:01:54,352
-One strawberry shaved ice, please. -Sure thing.

27
00:01:56,020 --> 00:01:59,023
Huh? Since when did you have an electric ice shaver?

28
00:01:59,232 --> 00:02:00,691
I just got it this year.

29
00:02:01,108 --> 00:02:04,529
Electric is so much easier, and now I won't hurt my shoulders.

30
00:02:04,737 --> 00:02:06,280
Well, I guess that's true.

31
00:02:07,740 --> 00:02:09,992
Oh, that? I'm throwing that out.

32
00:02:10,493 --> 00:02:13,496
You're throwing it out? What a waste.

33
00:02:13,704 --> 00:02:15,873
Hey, this thing still works.

34
00:02:16,082 --> 00:02:19,252
Yes, well, we all have to move with the times.

35
00:02:19,460 --> 00:02:20,586
Here you go.

36
00:02:21,254 --> 00:02:23,464
If you don't want it, can I have it?

37
00:02:23,673 --> 00:02:25,007
Go ahead.

38
00:02:25,216 --> 00:02:26,592
-Granny. -Hmm?

39
00:02:27,176 --> 00:02:29,345
-I want strawberry shaved ice. -I want melon!

40
00:02:29,720 --> 00:02:30,972
Sure thing.

41
00:02:34,392 --> 00:02:38,312
You kids keep wasting time instead of studying and your mom will go wild.

42
00:02:38,521 --> 00:02:41,148
Aren't you the one slacking off here?

43
00:02:41,899 --> 00:02:44,819
I'm not slacking off! I'm eating shaved ice!

44
00:02:47,405 --> 00:02:51,409
Damn kids these days. Even they're starting to sound like the chief.

45
00:02:55,997 --> 00:02:57,665
That was great. Time to go.

46
00:03:00,084 --> 00:03:02,712
Be sure to rug up tonight after eating something cold.

47
00:03:02,920 --> 00:03:05,798
Don't come crying to me if you get a tummy ache.

48
00:03:07,466 --> 00:03:08,426
Thanks for this.

49
00:03:08,634 --> 00:03:09,927
Sure thing.

50
00:03:14,724 --> 00:03:17,977
Hey there fellow workers, working in this hellish heat.

51
00:03:18,394 --> 00:03:20,104
Ryo-chan, what's that?

52
00:03:20,313 --> 00:03:23,566
It's an old ice shaver. I got it at the sweets shop.

53
00:03:23,774 --> 00:03:25,151
An ice shaver?

54
00:03:25,359 --> 00:03:27,987
You sure do get your hands on the weirdest things.

55
00:03:31,157 --> 00:03:33,242
What are you going to do with it?

56
00:03:33,451 --> 00:03:36,537
Huh? Isn't it obvious? I'm going to make shaved ice.

57
00:03:36,996 --> 00:03:38,205
Winter is mandarins,

58
00:03:38,414 --> 00:03:40,458
and summer is shaved ice.

59
00:03:41,125 --> 00:03:43,920
What else am I gonna do, shave fish flakes?

60
00:03:45,171 --> 00:03:46,964
If you wanted shaved ice...

61
00:03:47,173 --> 00:03:53,137
Why not use the penguin ice shaver you bought at that bargain sale last week?

62
00:03:54,972 --> 00:03:56,849
That old toy? Oh, please.

63
00:03:57,058 --> 00:04:00,353
In this era of fine dining, even shaved ice should be gourmet.

64
00:04:00,561 --> 00:04:03,481
Is there a proper way to make shaved ice?

65
00:04:03,689 --> 00:04:06,484
You just change your mind like the wind.

66
00:04:06,692 --> 00:04:10,529
You were so proud of this ice shaver and showing it off all last week.

67
00:04:10,738 --> 00:04:12,490
Hmph. I'm making shaved ice.

68
00:04:12,698 --> 00:04:17,286
Hey, Ryo-chan. I don't think real shaved ice is made with ice from a regular freezer.

69
00:04:17,620 --> 00:04:18,704
Huh?

70
00:04:19,038 --> 00:04:24,669
If you want it to be gourmet, it should be from Mont Blanc, or maybe even Antarctica.

71
00:04:25,211 --> 00:04:27,046
Antarctic ice, huh?

72
00:04:27,254 --> 00:04:30,174
My family has a business in Greenland,

73
00:04:30,383 --> 00:04:33,386
so if you don't mind Arctic, maybe we could do a deal?

74
00:04:34,387 --> 00:04:35,721
-That's it! -Huh?

75
00:04:35,930 --> 00:04:38,182
Arctic ice is far superior to Antarctic.

76
00:04:38,391 --> 00:04:40,559
I'll buy it! Fly it over, now!

77
00:04:41,018 --> 00:04:42,812
Uh... All right then.

78
00:04:43,604 --> 00:04:47,233
Call them right now! You know how much I hate waiting.

79
00:04:47,441 --> 00:04:48,401
Okay, I will.

80
00:04:48,609 --> 00:04:50,486
I'll go take a nap in the meantime.

81
00:04:52,196 --> 00:04:54,281
He's so quick to jump into things.

82
00:05:03,040 --> 00:05:06,544
What's all that racket? Can't sleep with all this noise.

83
00:05:08,170 --> 00:05:11,173
Ryotsu! The ice from the Arctic is here.

84
00:05:11,549 --> 00:05:14,552
Come on! Your ice is here.

85
00:05:16,178 --> 00:05:16,971
It's here!

86
00:05:17,388 --> 00:05:19,432
Where's my ice?

87
00:05:25,604 --> 00:05:27,606
It's a whole iceberg!

88
00:05:28,107 --> 00:05:31,027
Yes! And it's all mine.

89
00:05:31,360 --> 00:05:33,696
Here you go. 10,000 yen for the ice.

90
00:05:34,029 --> 00:05:34,905
Huh?

91
00:05:36,741 --> 00:05:38,617
This way! A little bit more!

92
00:05:41,495 --> 00:05:43,164
Yep, there's good!

93
00:05:44,915 --> 00:05:46,375
Yahoo!

94
00:05:48,669 --> 00:05:50,296
Now this is worth eating!

95
00:05:58,053 --> 00:06:00,181
I can't take it. It's so hot!

96
00:06:00,389 --> 00:06:03,726
And the AC just had to break on today of all days.

97
00:06:03,934 --> 00:06:06,103
Almost makes you want to wish for snow.

98
00:06:06,312 --> 00:06:07,229
That'd be nice.

99
00:06:10,983 --> 00:06:12,276
Whoa! What is that?

100
00:06:12,485 --> 00:06:14,236
Hit the brakes!

101
00:06:19,617 --> 00:06:21,535
-That iceberg! -It birthed a caveman!

102
00:06:22,286 --> 00:06:23,329
Oh, it's Ryotsu.

103
00:06:23,537 --> 00:06:24,955
Kankichi!

104
00:06:31,837 --> 00:06:34,298
Yep. Arctic ice just sparkles different.

105
00:06:34,507 --> 00:06:37,301
Hey, Ryo-chan. Can I have some?

106
00:06:37,676 --> 00:06:38,469
Not a chance.

107
00:06:38,677 --> 00:06:40,763
Why not? I only want a little bit.

108
00:06:40,971 --> 00:06:44,391
I paid out of my own pocket for this. Why should you get any?

109
00:06:44,600 --> 00:06:45,768
You scrooge.

110
00:06:45,976 --> 00:06:49,522
I already forked over 10,000 yen to Nakagawa.

111
00:06:49,730 --> 00:06:51,774
Every last bit of ice belongs to me!

112
00:06:51,982 --> 00:06:53,025
Jeez...

113
00:06:54,527 --> 00:06:58,447
Freezer ice is better suited to your penguin machine, anyway.

114
00:07:01,909 --> 00:07:04,078
What a crude sound.

115
00:07:05,204 --> 00:07:08,207
Mine, on the other hand, sounds absolutely divine.

116
00:07:08,624 --> 00:07:10,584
Like the gentle cry of a cricket.

117
00:07:10,793 --> 00:07:13,963
This is real Japanese shaved ice, I tell you.

118
00:07:14,171 --> 00:07:16,423
Now to just add a little syrup...

119
00:07:16,632 --> 00:07:17,633
and it's ready!

120
00:07:18,759 --> 00:07:22,096
The ice is as beautiful and delicate as freshly fallen snow.

121
00:07:22,972 --> 00:07:25,057
Let's try a mouthful.

122
00:07:26,642 --> 00:07:27,560
Yum!

123
00:07:28,936 --> 00:07:30,688
Nothing beats the real deal!

124
00:07:31,564 --> 00:07:33,482
But yours...

125
00:07:33,691 --> 00:07:37,987
Yours stinks like the inside of a fridge mixed with chlorinated tap water.

126
00:07:38,195 --> 00:07:40,114
Disgusting.

127
00:07:44,034 --> 00:07:47,705
A flavor so divine can only come from ice of the highest pedigree.

128
00:07:47,913 --> 00:07:51,500
Bold, yet delicate, and steeped in the romance of antiquity.

129
00:07:51,709 --> 00:07:54,628
It's the best of the best when it comes to shaved ice.

130
00:07:54,837 --> 00:07:58,757
No, in fact, to call anything else "shaved ice" would be blasphemy!

131
00:08:01,010 --> 00:08:05,556
Shaved ice made with freezer ice is no longer fit to be called "shaved ice."

132
00:08:05,764 --> 00:08:10,269
You literally had some from the penguin yesterday and you said it was the best.

133
00:08:11,228 --> 00:08:15,274
I know! I'll add some milk to the next one for a little extra luxury.

134
00:08:15,608 --> 00:08:16,400
Huh?

135
00:08:17,776 --> 00:08:18,819
Hey!

136
00:08:19,278 --> 00:08:21,197
Stop stealing my ice!

137
00:08:21,405 --> 00:08:22,323
I'll arrest you!

138
00:08:22,907 --> 00:08:24,533
Surely we can have a little bit?

139
00:08:24,742 --> 00:08:28,162
Thanks to your ice pile, we're stuck rerouting traffic in the heat.

140
00:08:28,370 --> 00:08:31,373
Look, they're honking at you! Go back to your job!

141
00:08:31,582 --> 00:08:32,416
Ah!

142
00:08:32,625 --> 00:08:33,584
You scrooge.

143
00:08:42,384 --> 00:08:43,385
It's so beautiful!

144
00:08:47,014 --> 00:08:52,269
Yum! Truly delicious! This is real gourmet shaved ice!

145
00:08:54,021 --> 00:08:57,441
Well, I wish you could taste it too.

146
00:08:57,650 --> 00:09:01,445
It's truly sad that you're satisfied with that inferior shaved ice.

147
00:09:01,904 --> 00:09:06,033
My ice positively shimmers with a silky, mellow taste.

148
00:09:06,367 --> 00:09:08,494
Even the crackling of the ice hums

149
00:09:08,702 --> 00:09:15,084
with the delicate whispers of Venus, roused from an ancient rest.

150
00:09:17,920 --> 00:09:22,216
Mmm! Fantastic! This world is rosy! It's the color of shaved ice!

151
00:09:23,634 --> 00:09:25,469
I'm going to stuff myself!

152
00:09:29,723 --> 00:09:31,809
My mouth is frozen numb.

153
00:09:33,435 --> 00:09:36,313
Wow, eating 17 bowls is enough to...

154
00:09:36,522 --> 00:09:37,940
Sick of shaved ice by now?

155
00:09:39,274 --> 00:09:41,443
As if!

156
00:09:43,237 --> 00:09:45,114
So this is the iceberg.

157
00:09:45,322 --> 00:09:46,865
It's really cold!

158
00:09:47,074 --> 00:09:48,325
Hey!

159
00:09:49,618 --> 00:09:50,911
Go away! It's not safe!

160
00:09:51,120 --> 00:09:53,497
But it feels so nice!

161
00:09:56,291 --> 00:09:57,835
Damn crows!

162
00:09:59,336 --> 00:10:02,047
Hey! That's my ice. Stop pecking at it!

163
00:10:02,589 --> 00:10:06,510
I forked out a lot of cash for this! This has to be my food for the next week!

164
00:10:13,267 --> 00:10:15,144
Now for a giant bowl of deliciousness!

165
00:10:15,352 --> 00:10:19,023
Strawberry flavored with a milk topping.

166
00:10:24,528 --> 00:10:27,364
I ate too fast and got a brain freeze!

167
00:10:30,576 --> 00:10:32,286
Are you all right?

168
00:10:32,494 --> 00:10:35,581
Don't force yourself. Why not share it with the neighborhood?

169
00:10:35,789 --> 00:10:37,583
T-This is nothing!

170
00:10:37,791 --> 00:10:40,294
It's just frozen water. I can handle all of it!

171
00:10:41,295 --> 00:10:44,465
After all, two thirds of the human body is made up of water.

172
00:10:45,299 --> 00:10:48,677
There's still so much left of just this one little piece.

173
00:10:49,428 --> 00:10:51,805
All right, I'll let you in on a little treat.

174
00:10:52,014 --> 00:10:54,308
You can have some of my gourmet shaved ice.

175
00:10:54,516 --> 00:10:56,310
I already ate, so I'm full.

176
00:10:56,518 --> 00:10:59,813
Right. We don't want any. This ice is your responsibility.

177
00:11:00,147 --> 00:11:02,608
Fine! I'll eat it all myself.

178
00:11:02,816 --> 00:11:04,318
No matter what!

179
00:11:14,745 --> 00:11:16,121
What are you going to do?

180
00:11:16,747 --> 00:11:19,083
Isn't it obvious? I'm gonna eat it.

181
00:11:19,291 --> 00:11:21,794
I'm just sick of strawberry and milk flavors.

182
00:11:22,336 --> 00:11:25,839
So, let's switch it up with some cola here, and some ketchup there.

183
00:11:26,048 --> 00:11:28,258
And an egg, and a bit of natto,

184
00:11:28,467 --> 00:11:31,053
and some vitamin drinks for extra nutrients!

185
00:11:31,261 --> 00:11:33,263
Well? Doesn't it look tasty?

186
00:11:33,806 --> 00:11:36,183
-You're really gonna eat that? -Of course!

187
00:11:40,312 --> 00:11:42,397
Just looking at it is making me want to puke.

188
00:11:50,489 --> 00:11:52,116
It's so cold!

189
00:11:52,783 --> 00:11:54,743
I need to warm up with some tea.

190
00:12:00,082 --> 00:12:01,959
All right! Now I'm all warmed up!

191
00:12:10,300 --> 00:12:13,095
That's it. I can't eat another bite.

192
00:12:13,303 --> 00:12:14,638
What about the rest?

193
00:12:15,514 --> 00:12:17,724
I'll make ice balls and eat them later.

194
00:12:17,933 --> 00:12:20,144
What's all this?!

195
00:12:21,228 --> 00:12:23,439
Ryotsu, is this your doing again?

196
00:12:23,897 --> 00:12:26,483
What are you talking about? I haven't done anything.

197
00:12:26,692 --> 00:12:28,235
You moron! Get over here!

198
00:12:28,444 --> 00:12:29,445
Ow! Ow! Ow!

199
00:12:29,653 --> 00:12:32,197
You're stretching my ear!

200
00:12:32,614 --> 00:12:34,074
What's with all this ice?

201
00:12:34,283 --> 00:12:36,743
Our phones are being bombarded with complaints!

202
00:12:36,952 --> 00:12:37,744
What?

203
00:12:38,370 --> 00:12:40,289
Well you see, um... This is...

204
00:12:40,497 --> 00:12:42,958
It's a stage set for you, Chief.

205
00:12:43,167 --> 00:12:44,251
For me, you say?

206
00:12:44,751 --> 00:12:45,961
That's right!

207
00:12:46,170 --> 00:12:50,007
We thought this iceberg would be the perfect backdrop

208
00:12:50,215 --> 00:12:52,217
for you to sing your favorite karaoke song.

209
00:12:52,426 --> 00:12:53,218
Don't play me!

210
00:12:55,429 --> 00:12:58,640
This is Arctic ice imported directly from Greenland, sir.

211
00:12:58,849 --> 00:13:02,060
Ryo-chan paid Kei-chan 10,000 yen for it.

212
00:13:02,269 --> 00:13:03,729
Ryotsu...

213
00:13:04,646 --> 00:13:06,148
Would you like some, Chief?

214
00:13:06,523 --> 00:13:08,025
I would not!

215
00:13:09,151 --> 00:13:10,485
Destroy this block of ice!

216
00:13:11,028 --> 00:13:12,946
You hear me? By the end of the day!

217
00:13:13,572 --> 00:13:15,741
By the end of the day? But...

218
00:13:15,991 --> 00:13:16,992
Silence!

219
00:13:17,284 --> 00:13:20,078
If it isn't completely gone by tomorrow morning,

220
00:13:20,329 --> 00:13:22,998
I'll transfer you to the Arctic myself!

221
00:13:23,207 --> 00:13:26,543
The Arctic? But there isn't even a police station there!

222
00:13:26,752 --> 00:13:28,837
I'll open one just for you.

223
00:13:29,046 --> 00:13:30,672
Got it?

224
00:13:44,228 --> 00:13:47,189
There's still so much left.

225
00:13:47,397 --> 00:13:50,734
It'll be impossible to eat all in one day.

226
00:13:50,943 --> 00:13:55,322
So, this is the iceberg you bought, is it?

227
00:13:55,531 --> 00:13:58,116
It's genuine ice from the Arctic.

228
00:13:58,325 --> 00:14:01,662
I'm not surprised people are talking about it. It stands out.

229
00:14:01,870 --> 00:14:04,122
What are you going to do with it?

230
00:14:04,331 --> 00:14:07,960
I was planning to turn it all into shaved ice so I could eat it.

231
00:14:08,502 --> 00:14:10,295
Shaved ice?!

232
00:14:10,546 --> 00:14:13,882
With that much shaved ice, you could make a ski slope.

233
00:14:15,509 --> 00:14:17,469
-That's it! What a great idea! -Huh?

234
00:14:17,761 --> 00:14:21,598
Skiing is just what we need for this stifling hot summer!

235
00:14:21,848 --> 00:14:23,850
This will work!

236
00:14:24,726 --> 00:14:28,063
"RYOTSU SNOWLAND"

237
00:14:28,272 --> 00:14:30,524
We can rent out skis and snowboards.

238
00:14:30,774 --> 00:14:32,609
Maybe even bobsleds!

239
00:14:33,944 --> 00:14:36,530
I'll make some money and get rid of the ice.

240
00:14:36,780 --> 00:14:38,156
Two birds, one stone!

241
00:14:38,365 --> 00:14:41,201
All right! Time to get to work!

242
00:14:47,583 --> 00:14:48,667
Let's do this.

243
00:14:56,883 --> 00:14:58,218
What's going on?

244
00:15:04,266 --> 00:15:06,893
I won't stop even if my arms fall off!

245
00:15:08,562 --> 00:15:10,939
What is he up to this time?

246
00:15:11,481 --> 00:15:13,483
Probably some get-rich-quick scheme.

247
00:15:13,734 --> 00:15:16,945
Ryo-chan only gets this fired up when it comes to making money.

248
00:15:34,212 --> 00:15:36,715
Good job! Keep bringing it in.

249
00:15:36,923 --> 00:15:39,217
Sure thing! Leave it to me.

250
00:15:39,885 --> 00:15:41,803
We do the sheet after this.

251
00:15:42,012 --> 00:15:42,971
Okay!

252
00:15:43,180 --> 00:15:44,681
This'll be no sweat!

253
00:15:53,815 --> 00:15:56,026
At least the road is freed up again.

254
00:15:56,360 --> 00:15:58,653
But what's he doing with all that ice?

255
00:16:06,286 --> 00:16:08,830
Nearly done.

256
00:16:13,710 --> 00:16:16,421
Ryo-san! I got the skis and snowboards!

257
00:16:17,130 --> 00:16:19,174
Great! You can leave them there.

258
00:16:19,383 --> 00:16:20,300
Okay!

259
00:16:23,136 --> 00:16:25,722
"SKIS 1,000 YEN, SNOWBOARDS 1,000 YEN, SLEDS 800 YEN"

260
00:16:26,348 --> 00:16:28,600
All right, everything is ready.

261
00:16:28,809 --> 00:16:30,727
Turned out pretty good, I'd say.

262
00:16:32,771 --> 00:16:34,564
Come one, come all!

263
00:16:34,773 --> 00:16:37,692
Ryotsu Snowland is now open!

264
00:16:38,402 --> 00:16:40,070
What's "Ryotsu Snowland?"

265
00:16:40,278 --> 00:16:42,364
Well, come and see!

266
00:16:42,572 --> 00:16:44,700
Katsushika snow on a hot summer day!

267
00:16:44,908 --> 00:16:48,161
A desert oasis right here in the city! An urban snow resort!

268
00:16:49,663 --> 00:16:52,332
On this hot summer day, we have skis, snowboards,

269
00:16:52,582 --> 00:16:55,502
and even bobsleds for you to enjoy!

270
00:16:55,710 --> 00:16:57,087
So, come on in!

271
00:16:57,295 --> 00:16:58,547
Let's go.

272
00:16:58,755 --> 00:17:00,215
Yeah, it looks fun!

273
00:17:00,424 --> 00:17:02,092
-Me first! -No, me!

274
00:17:03,218 --> 00:17:08,014
The traffic problem has been fixed, but there's still a lot of ice left.

275
00:17:08,807 --> 00:17:12,686
Okay, this is where you get your rentals. No bringing your own gear.

276
00:17:12,894 --> 00:17:14,813
Groups get a 10% discount.

277
00:17:15,021 --> 00:17:18,233
Little kids and the elderly get 30% off.

278
00:17:18,442 --> 00:17:19,443
How about it?

279
00:17:19,651 --> 00:17:21,695
-I'll take a snowboard. -Here you go.

280
00:17:23,113 --> 00:17:25,574
Welcome, welcome!

281
00:17:25,782 --> 00:17:26,783
Come on in!

282
00:17:27,534 --> 00:17:28,869
Thank you.

283
00:17:29,494 --> 00:17:31,788
Looks like I'll make a few million.

284
00:17:32,205 --> 00:17:34,082
I know! We need food stalls.

285
00:17:36,501 --> 00:17:38,253
Welcome one and all.

286
00:17:38,462 --> 00:17:41,631
For your empty bellies, try the famous Snowland Snow Sushi!

287
00:17:41,840 --> 00:17:44,259
For mom and dad, we have fresh tuna and squid.

288
00:17:44,468 --> 00:17:46,553
And for the kids, we also have egg!

289
00:17:47,471 --> 00:17:49,681
Don't leave without giving them a try!

290
00:17:49,931 --> 00:17:51,433
I'll take a tuna snow sushi.

291
00:17:51,641 --> 00:17:52,642
I'll have egg.

292
00:17:52,851 --> 00:17:55,061
All right, one tuna and one egg.

293
00:17:59,691 --> 00:18:00,484
Here you are!

294
00:18:01,067 --> 00:18:03,653
Hey, that's not rice. That's ice!

295
00:18:04,279 --> 00:18:06,823
That's right. It's cold, so it stays fresh longer.

296
00:18:07,032 --> 00:18:08,867
How do you eat it?

297
00:18:09,075 --> 00:18:12,662
With jam! Like this.

298
00:18:14,164 --> 00:18:15,874
Refreshing and delicious.

299
00:18:16,082 --> 00:18:17,667
Jam on sushi?

300
00:18:17,876 --> 00:18:22,130
If you'd prefer to have something cooked, we also have an Indian Ice Curry.

301
00:18:22,339 --> 00:18:23,215
Step right up!

302
00:18:23,423 --> 00:18:25,550
Curried ice too?

303
00:18:25,884 --> 00:18:27,219
I want one of those!

304
00:18:27,427 --> 00:18:28,678
One curry, coming up!

305
00:18:31,348 --> 00:18:33,642
I can go on forever!

306
00:18:39,439 --> 00:18:42,275
That's right! Whatever falls down is yours to keep.

307
00:18:42,484 --> 00:18:44,778
Just don't hit the cars or the eggs.

308
00:18:44,986 --> 00:18:47,906
Pitch it clean and straight!

309
00:18:48,114 --> 00:18:50,700
-Gimme one here, mister. -Me too! Me too!

310
00:18:50,909 --> 00:18:52,077
Okay, okay. Don't push.

311
00:18:52,285 --> 00:18:53,745
It's five balls for 200 yen!

312
00:18:54,371 --> 00:18:57,249
-I'll take five balls. -Ten for me!

313
00:18:57,874 --> 00:18:59,334
Sold out already.

314
00:18:59,543 --> 00:19:01,753
This business is genius!

315
00:19:05,715 --> 00:19:06,925
What?!

316
00:19:07,342 --> 00:19:08,468
What did you say?!

317
00:19:08,677 --> 00:19:09,928
Ryotsu did what?!

318
00:19:10,262 --> 00:19:12,931
He built a snow land in the park without permission.

319
00:19:13,139 --> 00:19:14,683
He's gathering a crowd.

320
00:19:15,350 --> 00:19:19,104
I hear he's renting out skis and snowboards to make money on the side.

321
00:19:19,312 --> 00:19:21,481
Seriously, what's wrong with him?!

322
00:19:22,816 --> 00:19:24,025
Look at all this.

323
00:19:24,234 --> 00:19:28,363
If I keep this up, maybe I should buy another iceberg.

324
00:19:28,572 --> 00:19:29,823
Ryotsu!

325
00:19:34,536 --> 00:19:36,121
W-What is it, Chief?

326
00:19:36,329 --> 00:19:41,251
I hear you're making money off something you built in the park without permission.

327
00:19:41,626 --> 00:19:42,836
Of course not!

328
00:19:43,044 --> 00:19:48,633
I just wanted to get rid of the ice, and get to know the locals a bit better.

329
00:19:48,842 --> 00:19:52,721
I wanted to make the Kameari residents happy, that's all.

330
00:19:53,555 --> 00:19:55,807
Then what do you call this?

331
00:19:57,309 --> 00:20:01,229
Ryotsu! I know you're hiding money behind your back right now.

332
00:20:01,438 --> 00:20:03,690
Return that money to the residents at once!

333
00:20:03,898 --> 00:20:05,483
N-No way!

334
00:20:06,693 --> 00:20:07,527
Hold it!

335
00:20:10,196 --> 00:20:10,989
Timeout!

336
00:20:11,197 --> 00:20:12,282
No timeouts!

337
00:20:12,490 --> 00:20:13,408
Stop!

338
00:20:17,787 --> 00:20:19,331
Got him!

339
00:20:22,125 --> 00:20:23,752
Ryotsu!

340
00:20:26,504 --> 00:20:29,257
Have some tuna! And squid! How about some egg?

341
00:20:32,802 --> 00:20:35,013
Ugh, wasabi?

342
00:20:38,850 --> 00:20:40,310
Get back here!

343
00:20:43,980 --> 00:20:45,273
Stop!

344
00:20:56,534 --> 00:20:57,494
Damn you!

345
00:20:58,036 --> 00:20:59,329
No! You can't!

346
00:21:02,290 --> 00:21:03,833
Earthquake!

347
00:21:05,251 --> 00:21:06,836
Stop!

348
00:21:10,465 --> 00:21:11,341
Ouch!

349
00:21:14,552 --> 00:21:15,845
Watch out!

350
00:21:21,101 --> 00:21:22,227
Damn it!

351
00:21:24,312 --> 00:21:27,148
This is my money! I'm not giving it to anyone!

352
00:21:29,943 --> 00:21:31,611
Why you!

353
00:21:36,157 --> 00:21:38,535
Prepare yourself, Ryotsu!

354
00:21:39,703 --> 00:21:40,704
No!

355
00:21:40,912 --> 00:21:42,288
Not so fast!

356
00:21:59,806 --> 00:22:01,099
It's going to collapse!

357
00:22:22,954 --> 00:22:24,372
What's that?

358
00:22:27,083 --> 00:22:30,545
Huh? Where did everybody go?

359
00:22:31,921 --> 00:22:33,798
And I'm supposed to clock off soon.

360
00:22:37,677 --> 00:22:39,846
Agh! Ryotsu!

361
00:22:43,266 --> 00:22:46,102
How strange. No one's here.

362
00:22:48,772 --> 00:22:50,315
Chief!

363
00:22:58,448 --> 00:23:00,492
Somebody save me!

364
00:23:13,004 --> 00:23:14,589
Help!

365
00:23:20,804 --> 00:23:22,722
Still got it!

366
00:23:24,432 --> 00:23:26,351
You will give everyone their money back.

367
00:23:26,559 --> 00:23:28,978
No! That's my money!

368
00:23:40,907 --> 00:23:43,493
What a good outcome. You used up all the ice.

369
00:23:43,910 --> 00:23:48,122
This is all because you're too stingy to let anything you buy go to waste.

370
00:23:48,331 --> 00:23:50,750
The man is who he is.

371
00:23:50,959 --> 00:23:51,835
Shut up!

372
00:23:52,043 --> 00:23:53,503
Ahh! Ow, ow, ow...

373
00:23:53,711 --> 00:23:57,173
TODAY'S DAMAGE REPORT

374
00:23:57,382 --> 00:23:59,926
TWO DOORS, TEN PAIRS OF SKIS, SEVERAL SNOWBOARDS

375
00:24:00,135 --> 00:24:02,303
ONE WINDOW, TWO DESKS, THREE LOCKERS

376
00:24:05,348 --> 00:24:06,808
Oh no, now you've done it!

377
00:24:07,016 --> 00:24:09,185
Good luck to anyone who gets Reiko mad!

378
00:24:09,602 --> 00:24:11,896
She'll send you and your patrol car flying,

379
00:24:12,105 --> 00:24:14,107
and even drive against traffic!

380
00:24:14,315 --> 00:24:16,985
It's no wonder she can't find a man!

381
00:24:17,193 --> 00:24:19,946
NEXT EPISODE REIKO'S ON THE HUNT!

382
00:24:20,155 --> 00:24:21,322
Don't miss it!

383
00:24:32,959 --> 00:24:37,213
Let's keep smiling always

384
00:24:37,881 --> 00:24:41,509
Even when things go wrong

385
00:24:41,718 --> 00:24:45,972
Keep a pretty smile on your face

386
00:24:46,598 --> 00:24:51,019
And go out as if nothing happened

387
00:24:51,561 --> 00:24:55,148
Hey, show me your smile

388
00:24:55,356 --> 00:24:59,277
You did nothing wrong

389
00:25:00,236 --> 00:25:03,823
Hey, show me your smile

390
00:25:04,032 --> 00:25:07,410
Just like you did before, yeah

391
00:25:07,911 --> 00:25:12,081
I want you to smile always

392
00:25:12,790 --> 00:25:17,253
A woman with a frown isn't pretty

393
00:25:17,754 --> 00:25:23,301
So you should smile as soon as you can

394
00:25:24,093 --> 00:25:27,055
It's the grown-up thing to do

395
00:25:39,150 --> 00:25:43,863
KOCHIKAME SEE YOU NEXT TIME!
